    "params": {
     "text": "# Retrofit an SVG a page is already wired to\n\nA designer sends back redrawn artwork. The page it replaces has popups, styles and links bound to the **old ids** \u2014 and the new export kept none of them.\n\nWhich is the easy half. The rooms that were `<rect id=\"room-lab\">` come back as anonymous `<path>` elements: no id to rename, no layer name to match on, nothing but a shape sitting where the old one sat. Every design tool does this, and it is why \"just diff the ids\" gets you nowhere.\n\nThis flow works out what the new artwork lost, hands the old ids back to the elements that survived \u2014 **writing one onto the elements that have none** \u2014 and shows you the page before and after, live, so you can click the popups yourself.\n\nNothing is guessed at silently, and nothing is out of your hands. The **Mapping** table lists every element of the new artwork beside the old one it was matched to \u2014 add a column of your own, type an id into any row, and that element gets it whatever the match decided (`-` means leave that one alone). It is on the dashboard too, so you can correct a pairing with the page in front of you and watch the popup come back.\n\n**Press F5**, then open the **Before / After** page.\n\nIt runs on a built-in sample as it stands. For your own files, set **Path** on the two Source File nodes \u2014 everything downstream follows.",
     "width": 520
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "svg_src_page",
    "type": "flograph.scripting.python_script",
    "pos": [
     -1700,
     -1300
    ],
    "params": {
     "sample": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Northgate Works \u2014 site plan</title>\n<style>\n  body { margin:0; background:#0b1220; color:#e2e8f0;\n         font:14px/1.5 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  header { padding:14px 18px; border-bottom:1px solid #1e293b; }\n  h1 { margin:0; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:.01em; }\n  p { margin:4px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:#94a3b8; }\n  a { color:#38bdf8; }\n  svg { display:block; margin:14px auto; }\n  .room { cursor:pointer; transition:filter .12s; }\n  .room:hover { filter:brightness(1.28); }\n  #pipe-main { stroke:#38bdf8; stroke-width:5; fill:none; stroke-dasharray:7 5; }\n  #popup { position:fixed; left:18px; bottom:18px; max-width:290px;\n           background:#111a2e; border:1px solid #334155; border-radius:10px;\n           padding:12px 14px; box-shadow:0 8px 26px rgba(0,0,0,.5); }\n  #popup[hidden] { display:none; }\n  #popup-title { font-size:13px; font-weight:650; color:#f1f5f9; }\n  #popup-body { margin:4px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:#94a3b8; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>Northgate Works \u2014 site plan</h1>\n  <p>Click a room or a valve. Jump to <a href=\"#zone-north\">Zone North</a>.</p>\n</header>\n\n<svg id=\"plan\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 320\" width=\"520\" height=\"320\">\n  <rect id=\"bg\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"520\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#0f172a\"/>\n  <g id=\"zone-north\" data-name=\"Zone North\">\n    <rect id=\"room-lab\" data-name=\"Lab\" class=\"room\" x=\"40\" y=\"48\" width=\"160\" height=\"88\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\"/>\n    <text id=\"label-lab\" x=\"56\" y=\"98\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Lab</text>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"zone-south\" data-name=\"Zone South\">\n    <rect id=\"room-office\" data-name=\"Office\" class=\"room\" x=\"40\" y=\"192\" width=\"160\" height=\"88\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0e7490\"/>\n    <text id=\"label-office\" x=\"56\" y=\"242\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Office</text>\n    <rect id=\"room-store\" data-name=\"Store\" class=\"room\" x=\"224\" y=\"192\" width=\"120\" height=\"88\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/>\n    <text id=\"label-store\" x=\"240\" y=\"242\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Store</text>\n    <rect id=\"room-plant\" data-name=\"Plant Room\" class=\"room\" x=\"368\" y=\"192\" width=\"112\" height=\"88\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#b45309\"/>\n    <text id=\"label-plant\" x=\"384\" y=\"242\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" font-size=\"14\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">Plant</text>\n  </g>\n  <path id=\"pipe-main\" d=\"M 120 136 L 120 164 L 424 164 L 424 192\"/>\n  <circle id=\"valve-a\" data-name=\"Valve A\" cx=\"224\" cy=\"164\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#38bdf8\"/>\n  <circle id=\"valve-b\" data-name=\"Valve B\" cx=\"352\" cy=\"164\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#38bdf8\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<div id=\"popup\" hidden>\n  <div id=\"popup-title\"></div>\n  <p id=\"popup-body\"></p>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n  function show(title, body) {\n    document.getElementById(\"popup-title\").textContent = title;\n    document.getElementById(\"popup-body\").textContent = body;\n    document.getElementById(\"popup\").hidden = false;\n  }\n  function hook(el, title, body) {\n    if (!el) { console.warn(\"site plan: element missing, popup dead\"); return; }\n    el.addEventListener(\"click\", function () { show(title, body); });\n  }\n\n  hook(document.getElementById(\"room-lab\"), \"Laboratory\", \"Bench 1-6. Fume cupboard serviced quarterly.\");\n  hook(document.querySelector(\"#room-office\"), \"Office\", \"12 desks, meeting room, comms cabinet B.\");\n  document.querySelectorAll(\"#room-store, #room-plant\").forEach(function (el) {\n    hook(el, el.getAttribute(\"data-name\"), \"Restricted access \u2014 key from the gatehouse.\");\n  });\n  hook(document.getElementById(\"valve-a\"), \"Valve A\", \"Isolates the north spur. Normally open.\");\n  hook(document.getElementById(\"valve-b\"), \"Valve B\", \"Isolates the plant feed. Normally closed.\");\n\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".room\").forEach(function (el) {\n    el.setAttribute(\"tabindex\", \"0\");\n  });\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
    },
    "code": "\"\"\"Source File\n\nReads the page or the artwork off disk. Leave Path blank and the node hands\non the Sample below instead, so the whole workflow runs the moment you open\nit \u2014 then point Path at your own file and everything downstream follows.\n\n`path` is passed on as well, because the preview needs a directory to\nresolve a page's stylesheets and scripts against.\n\"\"\"\nNODE = {\n    \"label\": \"Source File\",\n    \"category\": \"IO\",\n    \"inputs\": [],\n    \"outputs\": [(\"text\", \"string\"), (\"path\", \"string\")],\n}\nPARAMS = [\n    {\"name\": \"path\", \"type\": \"file_open\", \"label\": \"Path\", \"default\": \"\",\n     \"placeholder\": \"blank = use the sample below\"},\n    {\"name\": \"encoding\", \"type\": \"string\", \"label\": \"Encoding\",\n     \"default\": \"utf-8\"},\n    {\"name\": \"sample\", \"type\": \"text\", \"label\": \"Sample\",\n     \"default\": \"\", \"placeholder\": \"used only while Path is blank\"},\n]\n\n\ndef run(ctx):\n    from pathlib import Path\n\n    path = (ctx.params[\"path\"] or \"\").strip()\n    if not path:\n        sample = ctx.params[\"sample\"] or \"\"\n        if not sample.strip():\n            raise ValueError(\n                \"no Path set and the Sample is empty \u2014 choose a file, or \"\n                \"paste the markup into the Sample box\"\n            )\n        ctx.log(f\"no path set \u2014 using the sample ({len(sample):,} chars)\")\n        return {\"text\": sample, \"path\": \"\"}\n\n    file = Path(path).expanduser()\n    if not file.is_file():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no such file: {file}\")\n    text = file.read_text(encoding=(ctx.params[\"encoding\"] or \"utf-8\"),\n                          errors=\"replace\")\n    ctx.log(f\"read {len(text):,} chars from {file.name}\")\n    return {\"text\": text, \"path\": str(file.resolve())}\n",
    "label": "Page HTML"
   },
